 and Alaska's Republican-leaning fundamentals cut the other way", "Peltola's large fundraising edge, though heavy outside spending is attacking her"], "rationale": "Polling since August has Peltola ahead in most surveys, including a strong Fabrizio Ward poll, and markets price her near 75%, so the forecast tilts modestly toward Democrats despite Sullivan's incumbency and the state's Republican lean. The split in expert ratings (mostly Tossup, some Lean D, one Tilt R) supports a narrow Peltola edge rather than a true coin flip.", "watch": "Ranked-choice tabulation with third-place Dan J. Sullivan still on the ballot, plus the RCV measure itself, could shift where second-choice votes land and move the margin either way.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Dan Sullivan (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Alaska's Senate race pits incumbent Republican Dan Sullivan against Democrat Mary Peltola in a ranked-choice general election, with a third-place Republican, Dan J. Sullivan of Petersburg, still on the ballot. Polling since the August primary has mostly shown Peltola narrowly ahead, including a Fabrizio Ward survey with her up six and several Alaska Survey Research polls with her up two to four, though Republican-leaning pollsters show Sullivan leading. Expert raters are split between Tossup and Lean D, with one Tilt R.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5747, "margin": 0.87}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6663, "margin": 2.0}]}